From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work6_pr_fixes_use_quaran <>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 20:46:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] build/configs: Build the detector and quarantine in
 qemu/build_test

No configuration in the tree enabled CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_UAF, and mm_uaf.c
is only added to CSRCS when it is set. Every call site is behind an
ifdef as well, so nothing in continuous integration compiled a single
line of the feature, and the same is now true of the quarantine. A
build break in either would go unnoticed indefinitely.

qemu/build_test exists for compile coverage and already runs in the
integration matrix, so enable both options there with their defaults.
It is a build test configuration rather than a product one, which is
the right place for a detection feature that costs contiguous free
space. CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_HEAPINFO is already set there, which is also the
combination where the report carries the owning task and the allocating
address.
---
 build/configs/qemu/build_test/defconfig | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/configs/qemu/build_test/defconfig b/build/configs/qemu/build_test/defconfig
index 5ee478dd..1cacd8da 100644
--- a/build/configs/qemu/build_test/defconfig
+++ b/build/configs/qemu/build_test/defconfig
@@ -771,6 +771,14 @@ CONFIG_DEBUG_VERBOSE=y
 # CONFIG_ARCH_HAVE_HEAPCHECK is not set
 CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_HEAPINFO=y
 # CONFIG_DEBUG_CHECK_FRAGMENTATION is not set
+# CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_FREEINFO is not set
+CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_UAF=y
+CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_UAF_POISON_SIZE=64
+# CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_UAF_PANIC is not set
+CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_QUARANTINE=y
+CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_QUARANTINE_CHUNKS=32
+CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_QUARANTINE_BYTES=4096
+CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_QUARANTINE_MAX_SIZE=1024
 # CONFIG_DEBUG_IRQ is not set
 
 #
